@event renown_chance
# en: A Chance to Be Noticed
title [41fb8e] = 被注意到的机会
# en: {A gold-bordered notice in the entrance hall says the academy wants volunteers.|Another gold notice, and the crowd around it is bigger this time.|The gold notice again. People glance at you as they read it now.} {~Whoever stands up will be seen by the whole school.|The village is invited.|There's a prize, and there's the shame of losing in public.}
text [a87b9d] = {门厅里一张镶金边的告示说，学院在征集志愿者。|又一张金边告示，这次围观的人更多了。|又是金边告示。现在人们读它时会瞟你一眼。} {~站出来的人会被全校看到。|村里人也受邀了。|有奖品，也有当众失败的羞耻。}
# en: A noticeboard in the entrance hall crowded with announcements, one gold-bordered notice pinned dead centre, students jostling to read it.
scene [947222] = 门厅的告示板上挤满了通知，正中央钉着一张镶金边的告示，学生们挤着去看。
# en: Cast a spell before the school
opt.demonstrate.label [0e28c7] = 在全校面前施一道咒语
# en: Arcana, hard. Fame or embarrassment.
opt.demonstrate.hint [b4213a] = 奥术，困难。出名或出丑。
# en: You write your name on the list before you can think better of it.
opt.demonstrate.say.1 [d4ad55] = 你没来得及多想，就把名字写在了名单上。
# en: Enter the great debate
opt.debate.label [c11160] = 参加大辩论
# en: Lore, hard. The faculty will be listening.
opt.debate.hint [c454bd] = 学识，困难。教职员会在台下听着。
# en: You sign up for the debate. Your hands are shaking already.
opt.debate.say.1 [43d367] = 你报名参加了辩论。手已经在抖了。
# en: Perform at the village fair
opt.fair.label [54524e] = 在村里的集市上表演
# en: Charm and a spell. The village pays and remembers.
opt.fair.hint [e9a0c5] = 魅力加一道咒语。村里人会付钱，也会记住你。
# en: You put your name down for the village fair. Somebody will have to teach you to bow.
opt.fair.say.1 [86c4a5] = 你报名参加了村里的集市。得有人教你怎么鞠躬。
# en: Keep your head down
opt.pass.label [b59315] = 低调行事
# en: {~You read the notice and walk on. Fame can find someone else this term.|Not this time. You've got enough to do without an audience.}
opt.pass.say.1 [9a4879] = {~你读了告示，走开了。这学期，让名声去找别人吧。|这次算了。不需要观众，你要做的事已经够多了。}

@event renown_demonstration
# en: Before the Whole School
title [edcef6] = 在全校面前
# en: The whole school is in the Great Hall, and so is the faculty, and so, at the end, is the headmistress. You're in the middle of the floor. Your spell is the most ambitious thing you know. There's a long silence while everyone waits for you to begin.
text [91116c] = 全校都在大礼堂里，教职员也在，最后连院长也来了。你站在场地正中。你的咒语是你会的最有野心的东西。所有人都在等你开始，一片长长的寂静。
# en: The Great Hall packed to the rafters, every house at its table, a single student standing in the middle of the floor with a wand raised.
scene [923d71] = 大礼堂挤得水泄不通，各学院坐在各自的长桌旁，一个学生独自站在场地正中，举着魔杖。
# en: Cast the hardest thing you know
opt.left.label [4a80f8] = 施展你会的最难的咒语
# en: It works, beautifully, better than ever before. The hall is silent and then very loud. For a month, first-years point at you in corridors.
opt.left.say.1 [649754] = 它成功了，美得惊人，比以往任何一次都好。礼堂先是一片寂静，然后震耳欲聋。整整一个月，一年级生在走廊里对你指指点点。
# en: It fizzles in front of everyone, with a noise like a sad goose. The hall is very kind about it, which is unbearable. You'll be "the goose" until someone else fails.
opt.left.say.2 [1eb78c] = 它当着所有人的面熄了火，发出一声像伤心的鹅一样的声音。礼堂里的人对此非常体贴，这才叫人受不了。在别人出丑之前，你都会是“那只鹅”。
# en: Cast something safe, perfectly
opt.right.label [09f177] = 施一道稳妥的咒语，完美无缺
# en: Something simple, done flawlessly. Polite applause. Nobody will remember it, and nobody will laugh at you either.
opt.right.say.1 [492d38] = 简单的咒语，施得毫无瑕疵。礼貌的掌声。没人会记得，也没人会笑话你。

@event renown_debate
# en: The Great Debate
title [b747aa] = 大辩论
# en: The great debate: "That magic should be taught to anyone who asks." You've drawn the side you disagree with, against a fourth-year who has never lost. The faculty are in the front row. Thorne is taking notes.
text [055fb1] = 大辩论的辩题：“魔法应当传授给任何求学的人。”你抽到了自己不赞同的那一方，对手是一个从没输过的四年级生。教职员坐在第一排。索恩教授在做笔记。
# en: Two lecterns on a stage under banners, a student at one pointing emphatically, an older student at the other frowning, a packed hall of faces in the dark.
scene [deb5fb] = 旗帜下的舞台上有两个讲台，一个学生在一边激动地指点着，另一边一个年长的学生皱着眉，台下黑暗中坐满了人。
# en: Argue your side brilliantly anyway
opt.left.label [b2d090] = 照样把你那方辩得精彩
# en: You argue the side you don't believe so well that you half-believe it. The fourth-year concedes. Thorne, afterwards, says "Hm," twice, which has never happened.
opt.left.say.1 [93af97] = 你把自己不信的一方辩得太好，好到自己都信了一半。四年级生认输了。事后，索恩教授说了两次“嗯”，这从来没发生过。
# en: The fourth-year takes you apart, politely and completely. The hall applauds you for trying, which is the cruellest kind of applause.
opt.left.say.2 [709e30] = 四年级生客客气气、彻彻底底地把你驳倒了。全场为你的努力鼓掌，这是最残忍的一种掌声。
# en: Argue what you actually believe
opt.right.label [fa097f] = 说出你真正相信的
# en: You throw away the brief and argue your own side, which is against the rules. You lose on points and win the hall. Thorne writes something down, and you'll never know what.
opt.right.say.1 [76c0d1] = 你扔掉了辩稿，为自己的立场辩护，这是违反规则的。你按积分输了，却赢得了全场。索恩教授写下了什么，你永远不会知道写的是什么。

@event renown_village_fair
# en: Magic at the Fair
title [ba2f28] = 集市上的魔法
# en: The village fair has a stage, bunting and a crowd of farmers who have seen every trick there is. The village apprentices sit at the front, cross-legged, unimpressed in advance.
text [7d86f8] = 村里的集市有一个舞台、彩旗，还有一群见过所有把戏的农夫。村里的学徒们盘腿坐在最前面，还没开始就一脸不以为然。
# en: A small stage at a village fair under bunting, a student conjuring coloured lights over a crowd of apprentices and farmers.
scene [ce56eb] = 村集市彩旗下的一个小舞台，一个学生在一群学徒和农夫头顶变出彩色的光。
# en: Put on a real show
opt.left.label [a47725] = 来一场真正的表演
# en: Lights, a dancing hat, a dove that turns into a shower of petals. The apprentices whoop. The farmers pay for the hat trick twice. The village talks about it until harvest.
opt.left.say.1 [90cf71] = 彩光、一顶会跳舞的帽子、一只变成花瓣雨的鸽子。学徒们欢呼起来。农夫们为帽子戏法付了两次钱。全村一直谈论到收获季。
# en: The dove refuses to turn into anything and sits on your head. The apprentices love it; the farmers don't pay.
opt.left.say.2 [5b1927] = 鸽子拒绝变成任何东西，就蹲在你头上。学徒们很喜欢；农夫们没付钱。
# en: Do card tricks for the front row
opt.right.label [7a00f1] = 给前排变纸牌戏法
# en: You sit on the edge of the stage and do card tricks for the apprentices until your voice gives out. No fame to speak of. Half of them walk you to the gate.
opt.right.say.1 [45b3b7] = 你坐在舞台边上给学徒们变纸牌戏法，一直变到嗓子哑了。谈不上什么名声。有一半人一路送你到门口。

@event renown_ice_rescue
# en: A First-Year on the Ice
title [36cb5d] = 冰上的一年级生
# en: A first-year has gone through the ice on the lake. A crowd is shouting on the shore, and nobody is moving. You're nearest.
text [89d72c] = 一个一年级生掉进了湖里的冰窟窿。岸上一群人在喊，没人动。你离得最近。
# en: A small figure clinging to the edge of a broken patch of ice in the middle of a frozen lake, students shouting on the shore, a student running out across the ice.
scene [cb70d0] = 结冰的湖中央，一个小小的身影扒着一块碎冰的边缘，岸上的学生在喊，一个学生正冲上冰面。
# en: Go out on the ice
opt.left.label [4c1b80] = 到冰上去
# en: You crawl out flat on the ice and pull them free. By supper the whole school knows your name, and the first-year's mother writes you a letter you keep for ever.
opt.left.say.1 [e4cca1] = 你平趴在冰面上爬过去，把 TA 拉了出来。到晚饭时全校都知道了你的名字，那个一年级生的母亲给你写了一封信，你一直留着。
# en: The ice gives under you too. The prefects pull you both out with a ladder. You spend a week in the infirmary, a little famous, mostly frozen.
opt.left.say.2 [8de0f6] = 冰在你身下也裂了。级长们用梯子把你们俩拖了上来。你在医务室躺了一个星期，小有名气，主要是冻坏了。
# en: Run for the prefects
opt.right.label [770692] = 跑去找级长
# en: You run for help, and the prefects get there with ladders in time. Someone else is the hero. You were right, and you feel wrong about it all winter.
opt.right.say.1 [2c0c95] = 你跑去求救，级长们及时带着梯子赶到。英雄是别人。你做得对，可你一整个冬天都觉得不对劲。

@event renown_portrait
# en: A Portrait for the Hall
title [316b46] = 礼堂里的肖像
# en: The academy hangs a portrait of its most talked-about students in the long gallery each year, and someone has suggested you. The painter's fee is yours to pay, as is the custom. The other portraits are already watching you.
text [1c2fbd] = 学院每年会把最受热议的学生的肖像挂在长廊里，有人提名了你。按惯例，画师的酬金由你来付。其他肖像已经在看着你了。
# en: A painter's easel in a sunlit corridor, a half-finished portrait of a student in formal robes, the sitter trying very hard not to scratch their nose.
scene [136a0d] = 阳光明媚的走廊里立着一个画架，上面是一幅画了一半的穿礼袍的学生肖像，坐着的人正拼命忍住不去挠鼻子。
# en: Sit for it
opt.left.label [e61125] = 去当模特
# en: Six sittings, an itchy collar and a painter who hums. The portrait is good, if a little more heroic than you are. Passing it, first-years straighten their backs.
opt.left.say.1 [41686f] = 画了六次，领子扎人，画师一直在哼歌。肖像画得很好，只是比你本人英勇了一点。一年级生从它面前经过时，都会挺直腰板。
# en: Decline politely
opt.right.label [c5820d] = 礼貌地谢绝
# en: You decline. Your purse is grateful. The portrait that goes up instead is of someone who looks very pleased with themselves, and you find you don't mind at all.
opt.right.say.1 [1dcbbd] = 你谢绝了。你的钱袋很感激。挂上去的是另一个人的肖像，看起来对自己非常满意，而你发现自己一点也不介意。

@event renown_rumour
# en: A Rumour About You
title [e03f40] = 关于你的流言
# en: Being known has a price: there's a rumour about you going round the castle, untrue and a little bit funny, and it's in Nessa's gossip column by Friday. People stop talking when you walk in.
text [d8f51f] = 出名是有代价的：一则关于你的流言在城堡里传开了，不是真的，还有点好笑，星期五之前就上了内莎的八卦专栏。你一走进来，大家就不说话了。
# en: Two students whispering behind their hands in a corridor, a third walking past them with a stiff back, a crumpled gossip sheet on the floor.
scene [c72b51] = 走廊里两个学生捂着嘴窃窃私语，第三个学生挺直脊背从他们身边走过，地上丢着一张揉皱的八卦小报。
# en: Answer it in public
opt.left.label [2a7890] = 公开回应
# en: You laugh it off at supper, loudly and well, with a better story of your own. By Monday everyone's repeating yours instead.
opt.left.say.1 [6fad96] = 晚饭时你一笑置之，笑得响亮又漂亮，还讲了个更好的故事。到星期一，大家传的都是你那个了。
# en: You deny it too hard, and it sounds true. The rumour grows a second chapter. It'll pass. It takes a month.
opt.left.say.2 [de5cf2] = 你否认得太用力，听起来倒像真的。流言又长出了第二章。它会过去的。过了一个月。
# en: Ignore it
opt.right.label [e2ae0c] = 不理它
# en: You say nothing. It burns for a fortnight and then dies of boredom. You learn who repeated it, and remember.
opt.right.say.1 [e7e80e] = 你什么也没说。它热闹了两个星期，然后无聊死了。你知道了是谁在传，并记住了。

@event renown_patron_dinner
# en: Dinner With a Patron
title [939524] = 与资助人共进晚餐
# en: A wealthy patron of the academy has asked to meet "the students everyone's talking about", and you're one of them. Dinner is nine courses. The patron likes clever talk and has been known to fund a promising student's whole final year.
text [773d2a] = 学院的一位富有的资助人想见见“大家都在谈论的学生”，你就是其中之一。晚餐有九道菜。这位资助人喜欢机智的谈话，据说曾资助过一个有前途的学生整个最后一年的学业。
# en: A long candlelit dining table in a grand townhouse, a student in borrowed formal robes seated between a wealthy patron and a portrait of the patron.
scene [de7bac] = 一座豪华宅邸里长长的烛光餐桌，一个穿着借来的礼袍的学生坐在一位富有的资助人和资助人的画像之间。
# en: Be dazzling
opt.left.label [166f5f] = 光彩照人
# en: You're witty through eight courses and wise on the ninth. The patron sends you home with a purse "for books" and an invitation to come back next year.
opt.left.say.1 [00008d] = 前八道菜你妙语连珠，第九道时又显得睿智。资助人送你回去时塞给你一袋钱“买书用”，还邀请你明年再来。
# en: You use the wrong fork, then the wrong joke. The patron is kind and bored. You're not asked back.
opt.left.say.2 [0f38a6] = 你用错了叉子，然后讲错了笑话。资助人很和善，也很无聊。你没有再被邀请。
# en: Be honest about your struggles
opt.right.label [8dbca1] = 坦诚说出你的难处
# en: You talk plainly about money and work and exams. The patron listens, the only one at the table who does. A small purse arrives the next week with no letter, just a crest.
opt.right.say.1 [11822a] = 你坦白地谈起钱、工作和考试。资助人在听，是整张桌上唯一在听的人。下个星期寄来了一小袋钱，没有信，只有一枚纹章。
